## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)
- Hallucination detection and factual verification
- Multilingual adapters and shared encoders
- Privacy constraints and on-device PII prefiltering
- Latency optimization, streaming, drift detection, rollout, and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline wiring
async function summarizeChat(chat, userLocale) {
  // 1) On-device PII redaction
  const cleanChat = await redactPII(chat);

  // 2) Retrieve relevant context from KB
  const context = await retrieveContext(cleanChat);

  // 3) Generate summary with RAG
  const summary = await generateSummary(cleanChat, context, userLocale);

  // 4) Hallucination detection via cross-check
  const verification = await verifyAgainstKB(summary, context);

  // 5) Confidence gate
  if (verification.confidence < CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD) {
    return { status: 'blocked', reason: 'low_confidence' };
  }

  return { status: 'success', summary: verification.summary };
}
```

